{"title":"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Work_using_Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Work using Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(More_Algebraic_Approach)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (More Algebraic Approach)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Fakesolve)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Fakesolve)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the figure below, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> congruent semicircles lie on the diameter of a large semicircle, with their diameters covering the diameter of the large semicircle with no overlap. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the combined area of the small semicircles and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the area of the region inside the large semicircle but outside the semicircles. The ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/0/0a04f4e905bfccb0efbe137bc83a2e29f1f4165c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A:B$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/e/2fe44a1d316d97656f7f0b8e19593356c4f0e2d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:18$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/1/901531f4b527616e8cc1a1884115f9781f713e0f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(18,0)); draw(arc((9,0),9,0,180)); filldraw(arc((1,0),1,0,180)--cycle,gray(0.8)); filldraw(arc((3,0),1,0,180)--cycle,gray(0.8)); filldraw(arc((5,0),1,0,180)--cycle,gray(0.8)); filldraw(arc((7,0),1,0,180)--cycle,gray(0.8)); label(&quot;...&quot;,(9,0.5)); filldraw(arc((11,0),1,0,180)--cycle,gray(0.8)); filldraw(arc((13,0),1,0,180)--cycle,gray(0.8)); filldraw(arc((15,0),1,0,180)--cycle,gray(0.8)); filldraw(arc((17,0),1,0,180)--cycle,gray(0.8)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"128\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/e/23e375e9778246ae973b5e364c41025b91e7808e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 16 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 17 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 18 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 19 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Work_using_Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Work_using_Answer_Choices)\">Solution 1 (Work using Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Work using Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Use the answer choices and calculate them. The one that works is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/e/dfec95f2af198a95d197703f54478a0466e21d4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bold{\\boxed{\\text{(D)19}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~Flame_Thrower\n(NOTE: This is both not specific and not useful during a real test. Please skip to the next solution! :D)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28More_Algebraic_Approach.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(More_Algebraic_Approach)\">Solution 2 (More Algebraic Approach)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (More Algebraic Approach)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the number of semicircles be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and let the radius of each semicircle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. To find the total area of all of the small semicircles, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/3/833d7dae966923c675b5afd92db4ece87df6ee17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\cdot \\frac{\\pi \\cdot r^2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"66\" height=\"39\" />. \n</p><p>Next, we have to find the area of the larger semicircle. The radius of the large semicircle can be deduced to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d743c77c96e676102fca614c3c43498f1e77e4f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\cdot r$\" width=\"32\" height=\"8\" />. So, the area of the larger semicircle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/9/5998d2acbfab0c971a5cb3c3cfb9288ef85fd4c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi \\cdot n^2 \\cdot r^2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"74\" height=\"39\" />. \n</p><p>Now that we have found the area of both A and B, we can find the ratio. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/1/e816cc7cb94d546f95a088399a742b3daad7ec58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{A}{B}=\\frac{1}{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"38\" />, so part-to-whole ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317918633e843255d05d7b9a90c48117d01eca65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:19$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />. When we divide the area of the small semicircles combined by the area of the larger semicircles, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/d/83dacecc3f852b6d1fc31accf43e249930c0b27f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"37\" />. This is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/a/82af14ec3b9e94ddec3d6f2b112646bcfba6b974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />. By setting them equal, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8aeed81ffe5071b2d5d291bca220b3480da708cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />. This is our answer, which corresponds to choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/e/dfec95f2af198a95d197703f54478a0466e21d4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bold{\\boxed{\\text{(D)19}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>Solution by: Archimedes15\n</p><p><br />\nNote: using WLOG you could have just set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the beginning.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Fakesolve.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Fakesolve)\">Solution 3 (Fakesolve)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Fakesolve)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each small semicircle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb95624b80be880c7df276b897d44dffd6edab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{N^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"30\" height=\"38\" /> of the large semicircle. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> small semicircles make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/a/82af14ec3b9e94ddec3d6f2b112646bcfba6b974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> of the large one, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/1/8c1f4271c1764ec1d5ac971e40cdcbd194f9cd0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{N}{N^2} = \\frac1{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"38\" />. Solving this, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/6/3e6b4391f25789ac9419bc73abb91174108ef344.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />. \n</p><p>... Don't think this one works but it kinda does\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4KT0AtJZQzU\">https://youtu.be/4KT0AtJZQzU</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!!!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/qdyL6-Vmrrk\">https://youtu.be/qdyL6-Vmrrk</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/NsQbhYfGh1Q?t=1120\">https://youtu.be/NsQbhYfGh1Q?t=1120</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B\">2018 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017031027\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 245/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2320/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 154/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5364/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.488      1 -total\n 59.42%    8.014      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 39.70%    5.355      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15991:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017031027 and revision id 291571. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}